==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.|de}}  {{term|anatomia}}, from {{etyl|grc|de}} {{term|ἀνατομία|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|ἀνατομή|tr=anatome||dissection|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|ἀνά|tr=ana||up|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|τέμνω|tr=temnō||I cut, incise|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
'''Anatomie''' {{f}}

# {{biology|lang=de}} [[anatomy|Anatomy]], [[study]] of the [[structure]] of [[living]] [[being]]s.
# {{biology|lang=de}} [[dissection|Dissection]].
# {{biology|lang=de}} [[structural|Structural]] [[makeup]] of an [[organism]] or parts thereof.
# [[anatomy department|Anatomy department]], [[anatomical institute]].
# [[treatise|Treatise]] on the [[science]] of [[anatomy]].

